CFDApp

Usage:
  cfdapp --case <case-directory>
  cfdapp --case <dir> --checkpoint <file> [--checkpoint-every <n>]
  cfdapp --case <dir> --resume <file>

Options:
  --case <path>            Run a CFD case
  --checkpoint <file>      Write a solver checkpoint to <file>
  --checkpoint-every <n>   Also write it every n outer iterations
                           (requires --checkpoint; n >= 1)
  --resume <file>          Continue a solve from a checkpoint written
                           earlier for this same case and mesh
  --log-level <level>      Diagnostics verbosity on stderr: trace, debug, info, warning, error
                           (default info; results always go to stdout)
  --help                   Show help
  --version                Show version

A checkpoint stores solver state -- velocity, pressure, the corrected face
mass flux, the completed iteration count and the residual history -- so a
resumed run continues the same solve instead of starting a new one.
Resuming needs the same mesh and the same case configuration; only
solver.json max_iterations may differ, so a run can be given more
iterations and finished.
